  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Save Malnourished Children in Rural Indonesia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Malnutrition is still a nutritional problem in Indonesia. This is reflected in the prevalence of stunting under five, which is still at 24.4%. In order to improve the quality of superior and qualified human resources, we are targeting under-5 stunting to be 14% by the end of 2024. The results of the Indonesian Ministry of Health&apos;s Study on Nutritional Status (SSGI) show that 24.5% of infants under 5 years of age (toddlers) in West Java will experience stunting in 2022</narrative>
  </description>
